{"ts": "2026-10-30T04:35:08.095471Z", "run_id": "r-20261030T0434Z-57e9", "unit": "openspec:add-web-sign-in", "seq": 9, "type": "task.started", "task": "4.2", "title": "4.2 Write `test/support/e2e-stack/tenant-b-part.test.ts` first (begins with `assert.equal(typeof seedUsersOf, \"function\")`; `withTestDatabase()`; handles as in add-oidc-login's part test: a `database` handle with `api` `{ host: \"127.0.0.1\", port, database: db.name, ownerUrl: db.ownerUrl }` and the real `oidcPart` started with a hand-made `PartContext` in a temp directory; the default tenant from `ensureDefaultTenant(db.ownerPool, E2E_TENANT_NAME)` and `oidcPart.seed`; the three scenarios of that part, the first one also calling `ensureDefaultTenant(db.ownerPool, E2E_TENANT_NAME)` after the second seeds and comparing its `tenantId` with the one from before, the discovery one starting with `names.includes(\"tenant-b\")` and `existsSync` of the part file before it reads it; `handle.api` is cast to `SeedSource`), then implement `TENANT_B_NAME`, `TENANT_B_ORGANIZATION`, `SeedUser`, `seedUsersOf` and `tenantBPart` in `test/support/e2e-stack/tenant-b-part.ts` (decisions 11 and 12: `start` calls `databaseApi` and `oidcApi` first and returns `{ env: {}, api: { seedData: () => ({ users: seedUsersOf(fake) }) }, close }`; `seed` opens `createPool(ownerUrl, { max: 1, applicationName: \"e2e-tenant-b\" })`, runs `INSERT INTO ursitoare.tenant (tenant_id, name, review_profile) VALUES ($1, $2, 'solo') ON CONFLICT (tenant_id) DO NOTHING` with `TENANT_B_ID` of `test/support/tenants.ts` (the owner insert needs no tenant setting: `ursitoare.tenant` has RLS enabled but not forced (`src/db/migrations/0002_tenancy.sql:7`) and is a catalogue-global table), calls `provisionTenantIdp(pool, { tenantId: TENANT_B_ID, reviewProfile: \"solo\" }, { issuer: fake.issuer, organization: TENANT_B_ORGANIZATION }, { clock: fixedClock(\"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\") })` and ends the pool in `finally`; `seedUsersOf(fake)` maps alice, bob, carol and mallory to `SeedUser` with `password` from `fake.passwordOf`, `displayName` the `name` claim of `decodeJwt(fake.mintToken({ user, kind: \"id\" })).payload` (missing or not a string: `E2eStackError` `STACK_PART_INVALID`) and `tenantName` `TENANT_B_NAME` for mallory, else `E2E_TENANT_NAME`), and create `test/support/e2e-stack/parts/27-tenant-b.ts` with the single statement `export { tenantBPart as part } from \"../tenant-b-part.ts\";` (the only task that changes it), implementing requirement \"The e2e stack seeds tenant B and the browser users\""}
